-### Numbered Steps
-1. **Initialization**: If `ADAPTIVE_SAMPLING` is defined, initialize the DDA iterator with `DDAIter::init(m_org, m_dir, tMin, tMax, dims)` [S1, unofficial]. If not defined, initialize `t.x = max(tMin + next_cell_begin, tMin)` and `t.y = min(t.x + step, tMax)` [S1, unofficial].
-2. **Ray Marching Loop**: 
-   - **Adaptive Mode**: Compute macrocell coordinates `m_org = org * macrocell_spacings_rcp` and `m_dir = dir * macrocell_spacings_rcp` [S2, unofficial]. Perform DDA traversal over macrocells using `dda::dda3` [S2, unofficial]. For each interval `[t0, t1]`, calculate opacity upper bound `r = opacityUpperBound(self, cell)` [S1, unofficial]. If `fabsf(r) <= float_epsilon`, skip the cell and continue DDA [S1, unofficial]. Calculate adaptive step `ss = sample_size_scaler(adaptiveSamplingRate(step, r), t0, t1)` [S2, unofficial]. Initialize `t = vec2f(t0, min(t1, t0 + ss))` [S1, unofficial]. Loop while `t.y > t.x`: set `DDAIter::next_cell_begin = t.y - tMin`, call `body(t)`, update `t.x = t.y` and `t.y = min(t.x + ss, t1)` [S1, unofficial].
-   - **Non-Adaptive Mode**: Loop while `t.y > t.x`: set `next_cell_begin = t.y - tMin`, call `body(t)`, update `t.x = t.y` and `t.y = min(t.x + step, tMax)` [S1, unofficial]. Set `next_cell_begin = float_large` and return [S1, unofficial].
